    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This section describes how to send email with the Spring Framework."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The following JAR needs to be on the classpath of your application in order to use the Spring Framework’s email support:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The "
                      },
                      {
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "Jakarta Mail"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "link",
                        "target": "https://jakartaee.github.io/mail-api/"
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " library"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "This library is freely available on the web — for example, in Maven Central as "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "com.sun.mail:jakarta.mail"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ". Please make sure to use the latest 2.x version (which uses the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "jakarta.mail"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " package namespace) rather than Jakarta Mail 1.6.x (which uses the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "javax.mail"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " package namespace)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "sidebar",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Library dependencies"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The Spring Framework provides a helpful utility library for sending email that shields you from the specifics of the underlying mailing system and is responsible for low-level resource handling on behalf of the client."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.mail"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " package is the root level package for the Spring Framework’s email support. The central interface for sending emails is the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface. A simple value object that encapsulates the properties of a simple mail such as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "from"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "to"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (plus many others) is the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SimpleMailMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class. This package also contains a hierarchy of checked exceptions that provide a higher level of abstraction over the lower level mail system exceptions, with the root exception being "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MailException"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". See the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "javadoc"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/mail/MailException.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for more information on the rich mail exception hierarchy."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.mail.javamail.JavaMailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface adds specialized JavaMail features, such as MIME message support to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface (from which it inherits). "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JavaMailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " also provides a callback interface called "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.mail.javamail.MimeMessagePreparator"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for preparing a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MimeMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Assume that we have a business interface called "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "OrderManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./OrderManager[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Further assume that we have a requirement stating that an email message with an order number needs to be generated and sent to a customer who placed the relevant order."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The following example shows how to use "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MailSender"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " and "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "SimpleMailMessage"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " to send an email when someone places an order:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "include-code::./SimpleOrderManager[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The following example shows the bean definitions for the preceding code:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "include-code::./MailConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "mail-usage-simple",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Basic "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SimpleMailMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " Usage"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "This section describes another implementation of "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "OrderManager"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " that uses the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MimeMessagePreparator"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " callback interface. In the following example, the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "mailSender"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " property is of type "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JavaMailSender"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " so that we are able to use the JavaMail "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MimeMessage"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " class:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "import jakarta.mail.Message;\nimport jakarta.mail.MessagingException;\nimport jakarta.mail.internet.InternetAddress;\nimport jakarta.mail.internet.MimeMessage;\n\nimport jakarta.mail.internet.MimeMessage;\nimport org.springframework.mail.MailException;\nimport org.springframework.mail.javamail.JavaMailSender;\nimport org.springframework.mail.javamail.MimeMessagePreparator;\n\npublic class SimpleOrderManager implements OrderManager {\n\n\tprivate JavaMailSender mailSender;\n\n\tpublic void setMailSender(JavaMailSender mailSender) {\n\t\tthis.mailSender = mailSender;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void placeOrder(final Order order) {\n\t\t// Do the business calculations...\n\t\t// Call the collaborators to persist the order...\n\n\t\tMimeMessagePreparator preparator = new MimeMessagePreparator() {\n\t\t\tpublic void prepare(MimeMessage mimeMessage) throws Exception {\n\t\t\t\tmimeMessage.setRecipient(Message.RecipientType.TO,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tnew InternetAddress(order.getCustomer().getEmailAddress()));\n\t\t\t\tmimeMessage.setFrom(new InternetAddress(\"mail@mycompany.example\"));\n\t\t\t\tmimeMessage.setText(\"Dear \" + order.getCustomer().getFirstName() + \" \" +\n\t\t\t\t\t\torder.getCustomer().getLastName() + \", thanks for your order. \" +\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"Your order number is \" + order.getOrderNumber() + \".\");\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t};\n\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tthis.mailSender.send(preparator);\n\t\t}\n\t\tcatch (MailException ex) {\n\t\t\t// simply log it and go on...\n\t\t\tSystem.err.println(ex.getMessage());\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n}"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "java",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "admonition",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The mail code is a crosscutting concern and could well be a candidate for refactoring into a "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "custom Spring AOP aspect"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "core/aop.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ", which could then be run at appropriate joinpoints on the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "OrderManager"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " target."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null,
                "type": "note"
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The Spring Framework’s mail support ships with the standard JavaMail implementation. See the relevant javadoc for more information."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "mail-usage-mime",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Using "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JavaMailSender"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MimeMessagePreparator"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "mail-usage",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Usage"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A class that comes in pretty handy when dealing with JavaMail messages is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.mail.javamail.MimeMessageHelper"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which shields you from having to use the verbose JavaMail API. Using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MimeMessageHelper"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", it is pretty easy to create a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MimeMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "// of course you would use DI in any real-world cases\nJavaMailSenderImpl sender = new JavaMailSenderImpl();\nsender.setHost(\"mail.host.com\");\n\nMimeMessage message = sender.createMimeMessage();\nMimeMessageHelper helper = new MimeMessageHelper(message);\nhelper.setTo(\"test@host.com\");\nhelper.setText(\"Thank you for ordering!\");\n\nsender.send(message);"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Multipart email messages allow for both attachments and inline resources. Examples of inline resources include an image or a stylesheet that you want to use in your message but that you do not want displayed as an attachment."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "context": "paragraph",
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The following example shows you how to use the "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "MimeMessageHelper"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " to send an email with a single JPEG image attachment:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "roles": [],
                    "title": null
                  },
                  {
                    "context": "listing",
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JavaMailSenderImpl sender = new JavaMailSenderImpl();\nsender.setHost(\"mail.host.com\");\n\nMimeMessage message = sender.createMimeMessage();\n\n// use the true flag to indicate you need a multipart message\nMimeMessageHelper helper = new MimeMessageHelper(message, true);\nhelper.setTo(\"test@host.com\");\n\nhelper.setText(\"Check out this image!\");\n\n// let's attach the infamous windows Sample file (this time copied to c:/)\nFileSystemResource file = new FileSystemResource(new File(\"c:/Sample.jpg\"));\nhelper.addAttachment(\"CoolImage.jpg\", file);\n\nsender.send(message);"
                      }
                    ],
                    "language": "java",
                    "roles": [],
                    "title": null
                  }
                ],
                "context": "section",
                "id": "mail-javamail-mime-attachments-attachment",
                "level": 3,
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Attachments"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "context": "paragraph",
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The following example shows you how to use the "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "MimeMessageHelper"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " to send an email with an inline image:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "roles": [],
                    "title": null
                  },
                  {
                    "context": "listing",
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JavaMailSenderImpl sender = new JavaMailSenderImpl();\nsender.setHost(\"mail.host.com\");\n\nMimeMessage message = sender.createMimeMessage();\n\n// use the true flag to indicate you need a multipart message\nMimeMessageHelper helper = new MimeMessageHelper(message, true);\nhelper.setTo(\"test@host.com\");\n\n// use the true flag to indicate the text included is HTML\nhelper.setText(\"<html><body><img src='cid:identifier1234'></body></html>\", true);\n\n// let's include the infamous windows Sample file (this time copied to c:/)\nFileSystemResource res = new FileSystemResource(new File(\"c:/Sample.jpg\"));\nhelper.addInline(\"identifier1234\", res);\n\nsender.send(message);"
                      }
                    ],
                    "language": "java",
                    "roles": [],
                    "title": null
                  },
                  {
                    "context": "admonition",
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Inline resources are added to the "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "MimeMessage"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " by using the specified "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "Content-ID"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " ("
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "identifier1234"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " in the above example). The order in which you add the text and the resource are very important. Be sure to first add the text and then the resources. If you are doing it the other way around, it does not work."
                      }
                    ],
                    "roles": [],
                    "title": null,
