                "level": 3,
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Inline Resources"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "mail-javamail-mime-attachments",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Sending Attachments and Inline Resources"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The code in the examples shown in the previous sections explicitly created the content of the email message, by using methods calls such as "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "message.setText(..)"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ". This is fine for simple cases, and it is okay in the context of the aforementioned examples, where the intent was to show you the very basics of the API."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In your typical enterprise application, though, developers often do not create the content of email messages by using the previously shown approach for a number of reasons:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Creating HTML-based email content in Java code is tedious and error prone."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "There is no clear separation between display logic and business logic."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Changing the display structure of the email content requires writing Java code, recompiling, redeploying, and so on."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Typically, the approach taken to address these issues is to use a template library (such as FreeMarker) to define the display structure of email content. This leaves your code tasked only with creating the data that is to be rendered in the email template and sending the email. It is definitely a best practice when the content of your email messages becomes even moderately complex, and, with the Spring Framework’s support classes for FreeMarker, it becomes quite easy to do."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "mail-templates",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Creating Email Content by Using a Templating Library"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
